.TH BATTERYGUARD 8
.SH NAME
batteryguard \- power off before the battery is empty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B batteryguard
[
.B -c
.I percent
]
[
.B -g
.I seconds
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Batteryguard
reads the first battery of
.B /dev/battery
(see
.IR acpi (8))
every 30 seconds.
When its status is
.B critical
or its charge has fallen to
.I percent
(default 5, or
.B batterycrit
from
.IR plan9.ini (8)),
and it is neither charging nor idle (no AC), it says so on the console
and in a window of the newest window system
.RI ( wsys (4)
or
.IR rio (1),
by their
.B /srv
files and
.IR window (1)),
waits
.I seconds
(default 60) for AC, and then runs
.IR fshalt (8),
which halts the file servers and powers the machine off.
.PP
.I Termrc
starts it where there is a battery, unless
.B batteryguard=off
is in
.IR plan9.ini .
A low battery before that is shown by
.IR wbar (1).
.SH SOURCE
.B /rc/bin/batteryguard
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acpi (8),
.IR fshalt (8)
.SH BUGS
Only the first battery counts.
There is no suspend to fall back on.
.PP
